          "type": "turn",
          "question": "If a document refers to the J45 family, is that a code or a category?",
          "answer": "J45 is a category. In the ICD-10-CM classification, it covers asthma (source: coding-asthma-j45). It sits in Chapter 10, the respiratory system chapter (source: coding-icd10-chapter-10-respiratory).\n\nThe category is never used at three characters. The extra characters record two things that are combined:\n- **Severity:** mild intermittent, mild persistent, moderate persistent, severe persistent, or \"other and unspecified.\"\n- **State at the visit:** uncomplicated, with acute exacerbation, or with status asthmaticus.\n\nEvery combination of these exists as its own code (source: coding-asthma-j45). So a document that says \"J45\" alone is referring to the broad category, and a full code would be more specific.\n\nThe search results did not cover how these codes are chosen for a particular person, or what any severity level means clinically. For questions about a specific diagnosis or code, a clinician or a qualified medical coder is the right person to ask.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
